                        ],
                        "form": "lemans"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e074a9fe-04cd-3058-9ffc-157bca5ace82",
                        "entry_id": "950ce64b-3823-3d5e-91bb-dbc058d1137d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One beloved; a lover, a sweetheart of either sex (especially a secret lover; a gallant or mistress)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "da3da016-73d7-4076-a712-8b2d593580ce",
                                "sense_id": "e074a9fe-04cd-3058-9ffc-157bca5ace82",
                                "text": "Faire Venus seemde vnto his bed to bring\nHer, whom he waking euermore did weene,\nTo be the chastest flowre, that ay did spring\nOn earthly braunch, the daughter of a king,\nNow a loose Leman to vile seruice bound[…]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "48fc7245-b832-45ae-8f2b-8a6987e8868a",
                                "sense_id": "e074a9fe-04cd-3058-9ffc-157bca5ace82",
                                "text": "The prisoner I speak of is better booty—a jolly monk riding to visit his leman, an I may judge by his horse-gear and wearing apparel."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fe540cd8-f9e5-3abd-976d-9c7bbe94211e",
                        "entry_id": "950ce64b-3823-3d5e-91bb-dbc058d1137d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A paramour."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "often",
                            "pejorative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe617d73-710f-4eeb-a6a5-0ed8f1f9b194",
                                "sense_id": "fe540cd8-f9e5-3abd-976d-9c7bbe94211e",
                                "text": "'...They are lost, I tell thee, they are lost. For them there is no heaven nor hell, and in neither shall they praise God’s name.’\n‘Father,’ cried the young Fisherman, ‘thou knowest not what thou sayest. Once in my net I snared the daughter of a King. She is fairer than the morning star, and whiter than the moon. For her body I would give my soul, and for her love I would surrender heaven. Tell me what I ask of thee, and let me go in peace.’\n‘Away! Away!’ cried the Priest: ‘thy leman is lost, and thou shalt be lost with her.’\nAnd he gave him no blessing, but drove him from his door."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c72baca2-48ae-4548-b194-c10db271845f",
                                "sense_id": "fe540cd8-f9e5-3abd-976d-9c7bbe94211e",
                                "text": "And he sent the news to William the Lyon, sitting drinking the wine and fondling his bonny lemans in Edinburgh Town, and William made him the Knight of Kinraddie[…]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
